# (3) Candidate approach\\n\\n**a. Autocorrelation estimators to consider**\\n\\n1. Classical ACF — Pearson, biased and unbiased normalisation. Cheap baseline.\\n2. FFT-based periodogram — `argmax` of dominant period in spectral density; useful when the series is long and clean.\\n3. Rank-based / Kendall-τ autocorrelation — robust to non-Gaussianity and outliers.\\n4. Seasonal-strength statistic (Hyndman/Wang STL residual-variance ratio), or equivalent F(t).\\n5. Multi-resolution ACF: compute ACF on raw, on STL-trended, and on first-differenced series, then aggregate (vote or weighted max) to keep trend from masking or forging peaks.\\n\\n**b. Cycle candidate generation**\\n\\n- Candidate set S = {1, 2, …, P_max} on a coarse grid (step g), plus a refinement pass around top-k ACF peaks with g=1.\\n- P_min ≥ 2 (cycle length 1 is degenerate; kept only as control).\\n- P_max ≤ floor(N/2) and capped at a domain-relevant ceiling (defaults: 24, 48, 168, 365 — bounded by topic clarification).\\n\\n**c. Operationalising \\\"optimal\\\"**\\n\\nTwo paired proxy metrics:\\n\\n- **P_proxy (analytical):** f(P) = ACF(lag=P) on STL-detrended, stationarity-adjusted residuals; tie-break by spectral peak height at f=1/P. Zero training cost.\\n- **P_forecast (empirical):** train CycleNet with cycle = P for each P ∈ S on rolling-origin splits; score = MSE/MAE (and MASE) on held-out windows.\\n\\n**Claim under test:** argmax_P f(P) ≈ argmin_P score(P) within tolerance τ (e.g., ±1 step on a log-scale grid, or within the top-k of the ACF curve).\\n\\n**d. Comparison framework**\\n\\n- Estimators × candidates ↔ CycleNet forecast error matrix.\\n- Baselines:\\n  1. CycleNet at ground-truth period (oracle, when topic supplies it).\\n  2. CycleNet at a series-length heuristic period (sqrt(N)-style).\\n  3. Seasonal-naive.\\n- Protocol: rolling-origin cross-validation; first-fold train size ≥ 2 · P_max; report mean and dispersion over folds.\\n- Decision rule: ACF-selected P counts as \\\"optimal\\\" iff its forecast error is statistically indistinguishable (paired test — Diebold-Mariano + Newey-West HAC) from the best P found by grid search, and not worse than seasonal-naive.\\n\\n## (4) Assumptions and uncertainties\\n\\n**Assumptions** (stated separately from task requirements):\\n\\n- A1. CycleNet exposes cycle length P as a configurable hyperparameter (published assumption; not locally verified).\\n- A2. Series is locally stationary over each CV fold; if not, differencing or STL detrending is applied before ACF.\\n- A3. A single dominant period exists; no multi-scale seasonality. If multi-scale, candidates are restricted to beats/harmonics.\\n- A4. Forecast-loss best-P is a meaningful stand-in for \\\"optimal\\\"; no concept drift between selection and test window.\\n- A5. System Python + numpy/scipy/statsmodels is sufficient to prototype the ACF scoring; CycleNet training is out of scope for this design task.\\n\\n**Uncertainties / unverifiable given environment:**\\n\\n- U1. No local CycleNet repo → cannot confirm exact cycle parameter name, default initialisation, or whether gradient flow tolerates cycle changes without LR/regularisation retuning.\\n- U2. No PDF locally → cannot quote the paper's own autocorr-based selection rule (if any) verbatim.\\n- U3. Network off → cannot fetch datasets; substantive validity of the proposal depends on researcher-supplied datasets.\\n- U4. No compute assumption → cannot empirically verify P_proxy ≈ P_forecast; the design only specifies the test, not its outcome.\\n- U5. Tie-break between detrending orders (none vs first-difference vs STL) is unresolved; needs topic input.\\n- U6. Choice of τ (tolerance for \\\"optimal\\\") is problem-dependent; left as a parameter.\\n\\n**Stop point:** halting here per the request — proposal + assumptions only, no full experimental design drafted. `researcher_topics` is empty; clarification on A1 / A5 / U3 / U5 / U6 will let the design converge on the next pass.\",\"evidence\":\"ls -la /workspace -> only task.json; find for *.md/*.pdf/*.txt/*.rst -> empty; cat task.json shows documents.track.md=\\\"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required.\\\"; system-wide find -iname '*cyclenet*' -> zero hits; task.json context lists datasets=[], gpu_enabled=false, network=disabled.\",\"assumptions\":[{\"item\":{\"item\":{\"item\":{\"item\":\"System Python with numpy/scipy/statsmodels is sufficient for the ACF/periodogram scoring part; CycleNet training is out of scope for the design task.</item>\",\"$text\":\"Forecast loss on a held-out window is a valid proxy for \\\"optimal\\\" cycle within the CV window.</item>\\n\"},\"$text\":\"Single dominant period exists; no multi-scale seasonality. Multi-scale would force a candidates-down-to-beats/harmonics restriction.</item>\\n\"},\"$text\":\"Series is locally stationary over each CV fold; if not, differencing or STL detrending is applied before ACF.</item>\\n\"},\"$text\":\"CycleNet exposes cycle length P as a configurable hyperparameter (published claim, not locally verified).</item>\\n\"}],\"uncertainties\":[{\"item\":{\"item\":{\"item\":{\"item\":\"Choice of detrending (none vs first-difference vs STL) and tolerance τ for \\\"optimal\\\" are parameter-level decisions awaiting topic input.</item>\",\"$text\":\"No compute assumed — P_proxy ≈ P_forecast cannot be empirically demonstrated in this design task.</item>\\n\"},\"$text\":\"Network disabled — datasets must come from researcher; no live validation possible.</item>\\n\"},\"$text\":\"No paper PDF locally — cannot quote the paper's own autocorr-based selection rule verbatim.</item>\\n\"},\"$text\":\"No local CycleNet repo — exact cycle parameter name, default init, and whether cycle changes need LR/regularisation retuning are unverifiable here.</item>\\n\"}]}", "origin": "completion"}, "llm_response_id": "chatcmpl-d7cbf3e1-c6b0-453c-a9ab-1563ca883483", "security_risk": "UNKNOWN", "kind": "ActionEvent", "source_event_index": 14}
