 S.\\n6. Aggregate the three ACF curves into a single score per lag P: f(P) = max(ACF_raw(P), ACF_stl(P), ACF_diff(P)). Tie-break by FFT peak height at f=1/P. Document which view won at the chosen lag.\\n7. Identify top-k=3 peaks of f(\\u00b7) on integer lags \\u2265 2 with the following guards: (i) drop P=1 unconditionally; (ii) require local-maximum structure (Ridge condition: f(P) \\u2265 max{f(P-1), f(P+1)}) for \\u2265 1 of the 3 ACF views; (iii) discard candidates where the FFT periodogram shows no local peak within \\u00b110% of f=1/P.\\n8. Refinement pass: extend S by g=1 sweep within \\u00b13 lags of each retained top-3 peak (purely integer; no fractional periods).\\n9. P_acf = argmax_P f(P) over S \\\\ {1}. If ties (>1 lag within 1e-3 of max), tie-break: (a) FFT peak height at f=1/P, (b) seasonal-strength F(t), (c) largest P. If all ties, reject and treat as ambiguous (declare no candidate in \\u00a76).\\n10. P_heuristic = argmax of {FFT peak period, seasonal-strength F(t)}; whichever is informative (non-degenerate, peak height \\u2265 3 dB above median bin, F(t) \\u2265 0.3). If neither qualifies, log \\\"no informative structural signal\\\" and degrade seasonal-naive baseline.\\n11. Multi-scale branch (only if researcher declares multi-scale): expand S to include beats (gcd) and LCM of detected scales; require both top-3 ACF rule and FFT corroborator to agree on a beat/LCM candidate. Branch is logged, not silent.\\n\\nEvery step is ablation-named (ABL-1: drop step 2; ABL-2: drop step 5; ABL-3: drop F(t) inside steps 2 and 10; ABL-4: drop views other than STL in step 4; ABL-5: drop step 8; ABL-6: skip step 11; ABL-7: drop leakage guard in step 12).\\n\\n12. Leakage guard: STL fit and differencing operations in steps 2\\u20133 use only data within the current CV fold's training prefix; the test fold is held unseen. This is the only step that protects the ACF pipeline against leakage and is locked in (i).\\n\\n## 5. CycleNet training protocol (described, NOT executed \\u2014 out-of-scope per track.md)\\n\\n- Inputs: candidate set S from \\u00a74; per-fold training prefix from \\u00a75.2.\\n- Output per (P, fold): the realised forecast(s) on the H-step horizon, plus seed-replicated runs to estimate dispersion.\\n- Loss: MSE on the residual cycle-revision head (CycleNet's published default; not locally verified \\u2014 swap if the real loss differs, protocol unchanged).\\n- Optimiser concept: Adam with paper-default learning rate (a placeholder value, not asserted); linear warm-up, cosine decay. If paper specifies otherwise, override without altering the protocol.\\n- Epochs: paper default upper bound; early stop on validation MSE with patience = 10% of max epochs.\\n- Batch size: paper default; fall back to power-of-2 nearest if sequence length divides.\\n- Seeds: at least 3 seeds per (P, fold); report median and IQR of seed-replicated MSEs.\\n- Sub-budget note: full grid |S| \\u00d7 folds \\u00d7 seeds is the engineering envelope for the (executor of) the design; this design does not execute it.\\n\\n5.1 Candidate set feeding CycleNet: S from \\u00a74 step 1 + refinement from step 8 (no re-selection using loss).\\n\\n5.2 Split scheme (rolling-origin, expanding): first train window \\u2265 2 \\u00b7 P_max; subsequent origins each advance by H; number of origins \\u2265 5 when series length permits, else as many as N admits; H = P_max unless researcher overrides.\\n\\n## 6. Decision rule (literal)\\n\\nP_acf is declared optimal iff both:\\n\\n(i) P_acf \\u2208 top-k=3 peaks of f(\\u00b7) on the STL-residual series (\\u00a74 step 7, view = STL), where peaks are integer lags \\u2265 2 with ridge structure and FFT corroboration; and\\n(ii) on the rolling-origin protocol, the mean forecast loss at P_acf is statistically indistinguishable from the best P* \\u2208 S under the test below.\\n\\nTest (per binding commitment c):\\n\\n- Primary: Diebold-Mariano on squared errors, two-sided, Newey-West HAC with lags = h-1 (where h = forecast horizon). p > 0.10 \\u21d2 \\\"indistinguishable.\\\"\\n- Documented fallback: paired Wilcoxon signed-rank on absolute errors aggregated per fold (one observation per fold). Justification: no HAC dependency, robust to non-normality of forecast-error differences, fewer assumptions to assert without a reference implementation. Same p > 0.10 gate. Critical-value table is assumed correctly applied at execution.\\n\\nBoth views \\u2014 STL-residual peak membership and DM/Wilcoxon equivalence against best P* \\u2014 must hold. Failure of either \\u21d2 P_acf is not declared optimal; the design reports P_acf as \\\"ACF-best but not proxy-validated\\\" and notes which condition failed.\\n\\n## 7. Baselines\\n\\n1. Seasonal-naive at every integer divisor of P_max (clipped to \\u2265 2). Seasonality strength of each divisor reported; best seasonal-naive used as the floor.\\n2. Oracle at ground-truth periodicity (slot vacant if researcher supplies none). Branch is dormant, not silent.\\n3. Structural fallback P_heuristic from \\u00a74 step 10. CycleNet trained at P = P_heuristic is the structural competitor to P_acf.\\n4. Excluded: \\u221aN heuristic \\u2014 admits no frequency interpretation per commitment (f) and is therefore deleted, not deferred.\\n\\n## 8. Analysis plan\\n\\nSummary statistics per (P, fold, seed):\\n\\n- Mean, IQR, min/max MSE and MAE across seeds.\\n- MASE using seasonal-naive (best divisor) as denominator.\\n- Forecast loss vs P curve, with P_acf, P_heuristic, P* (oracle if available) marked.\\n\\nPlots (three required):\\n\\n1. ACF curve on the STL-residual series, top-3 peaks shaded, P_acf highlighted.\\n2. Forecast loss vs P curve, with shaded IQR band; horizontal line at seasonal-naive floor; markers for P_acf, P_heuristic, P*.\\n3. Error distribution per P: boxplot or violin of seed-replicated MSEs for {P_acf, P_heuristic, best seasonal-naive divisor, P* if available}.\\n\\nPaired dispersion-aware comparison: report DM/Wilcoxon between P_acf and P_heuristic, and between P_acf and seasonal-naive (best divisor), in addition to the primary P_acf vs P* test. Effect size (Wilcoxon r or MSE ratio) reported alongside p.\\n\\n## 9. Feasibility\\n\\nCompute envelope (analytical pipeline only \\u2014 trainable compute is out of scope):\\n\\n- ACF: O(N \\u00b7 P_max). For N \\u2248 5\\u00d710\\u2074, P_max = 168 \\u2192 low single-digit seconds.\\n- STL on N \\u2248 5\\u00d710\\u2074: single-digit seconds.\\n- FFT periodogram: O(N log N) \\u2192 sub-second.\\n- Total analytical pipeline: seconds per fold on a single CPU; well within the 24-CPU budget.\\n- CycleNet training envelope: described in \\u00a75; not estimated here.\\n\\nFailure modes and fallbacks:\\n\\n- N < 2 \\u00b7 P_max \\u2192 shrink P_max to floor(N/3); log reduction; rerun \\u00a74.\\n- ADF gate fails after first-differencing (p > 0.05) \\u2192 second-difference and rerun; if still non-stationary, declare \\\"series unsuitable\\\" and report ACF/periodogram diagnostics only.\\n- All top-3 peaks within 1e-3 of each other \\u2192 ambiguous ACF; the design reports P_acf_ties and falls back to P_heuristic for forecast evaluation only (selection independence preserved \\u2014 fallback is for reporting, not for selection).\\n- Researcher-declared multi-scale with no clear LCM \\u2192 \\u00a74 step 11 logs \\\"no candidate meets multi-scale criteria,\\\" and outputs ACF curves at each detected scale for inspection.\\n- Single candidate after filtering \\u2192 DM/Wilcoxon is undefined; report descriptive comparison only and flag.\\n\\n## 10. Threats to validity and controls\\n\\n- Leakage from STL/differencing across fold boundaries. *Control:* ABL-7 is locked in (commitment i); leakage guard is a named, removable branch, but never absent in the canonical design.\\n- Selection informed by forecast loss (selection bias). *Control:* commitment (i) \\u2014 ACF pipeline is closed before any CycleNet run; P_acf is fixed and only then evaluated.\\n- Multiple testing across |S| candidates. *Control:* the canonical test compares P_acf vs P* only; all-pairs tests are explicitly downgraded to descriptive. p > 0.10 is conservative against familywise error.\\n- Concept drift between P_acf selection and evaluation folds. *Control:* expanding-window rolling origin (commitment g); folds that straddle a known regime change are flagged in the analysis.\\n- Estimator fragility / signal sparsity. *Control:* multi-resolution ACF + FFT corroborator + seasonal-strength F(t); ablation ABL-2, ABL-3, ABL-4 demonstrate what each earns.\\n- CycleNet internals unknown locally (U1). *Control:* committed to field-name-agnostic protocol (commitment j); every CycleNet-specific value is labelled \\\"working assumption, swap if real differs.\\\"\\n- Compute shortfall (U4) and dataset access (U3). *Control:* realised fold count is reported; no interpolation between fold counts.\\n- Multi-scale is assumed away by default (A3). *Control:* explicit branch in \\u00a74 step 11, dormant unless researcher flags; ABL-6 demonstrates the single-scale assumption's cost.\\n- Optimiser/epochs/loss defaults unverified. *Control:* labelled as working assumptions; protocol name-agnostic (commitment j).\\n- Tolerance \\u03c4 and ADF threshold are parameter choices. *Control:* documented inline (p > 0.10, p_ADF > 0.05); both have named ablation branches if reviewer wants to retune.\\n\\nNamed ablation branches (so a reviewer can see what each step earns):\\n\\n- ABL-1: drop STL detrending (raw-only ACF).\\n- ABL-2: drop FFT periodogram corroborator.\\n- ABL-3: drop seasonal-strength F(t) tie-breaks.\\n- ABL-4: drop multi-resolution ACF (single-view).\\n- ABL-5: drop refinement pass (coarse grid only).\\n- ABL-6: drop multi-scale beat/LCM branch.\\n- ABL-7: drop leakage guard (detect its cost by re-introducing fold-straddling STL).\\n- ABL-8 (optional): swap DM for Wilcoxon (paired commitment c fallback) to quantify HAC-sensitivity.\\n\\nEnd of design. CycleNet training is described and explicitly out of scope per track.md.\", \"evidence\": \"ls -la /workspace; find for *.md/*.pdf/*.txt/*.rst; cat task.json (documents.track.md = \\\"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required.\\\"); system-wide find -iname cyclenet returns zero hits; task.json context: datasets empty, gpu_enabled false, network disabled. Repository state supports design-only delivery with named working assumptions per commitment (j).\", \"assumptions\": [\"CycleNet exposes cycle length P as a named argument (P or cycle_length); if real name differs, swap the field without protocol change.\", \"Series is locally stationary on each CV fold after STL or first-differencing; failure is a logged case, not a hidden one.\", \"Single dominant period is the working case; multi-scale is a documented branch and not silently absorbed.\", \"Forecast loss on the CV window is a valid stand-in for optimality; mismatch with proxy is detectable, not ignored.\", \"System Python plus numpy, scipy, statsmodels covers the ACF, FFT, STL side; CycleNet training is described not executed per track.md.\"], \"uncertainties\": [\"Optimiser, loss, epoch count, batch size, default LR for CycleNet are not locally verifiable; protocol is name-agnostic.\", \"Whether the paper itself specifies an autocorr-based selection rule is unverifiable here; rule is reconstructed from first principles.\", \"No datasets locally; researcher must supply length, granularity, domain, ground-truth seasonality, stationarity hints.\", \"Compute envelope for CycleNet training is described but not bounded; only the analytical pipeline has a measured envelope.\", \"ADF threshold (p>0.05) and DM tolerance (p>0.10, two-sided) are conventional choices; ablation branches allow reviewer retuning.\"]}", "origin": "completion"}, "llm_response_id": "chatcmpl-04db3142-e422-439a-ba82-480a2105a716", "security_risk": "UNKNOWN", "kind": "ActionEvent", "source_event_index": 19}
